`result.setSourceEncoding(getReportProperty (properties, type, IReportProperties.SOURCE_ENCODING, false, false));`
Reason: The property key constants `OUTPUT_ENCODING`/`SOURCE_ENCODING` were defined with non-standard names (e.g. `"html.outputEncoding"`) that did not match the actual user-configured property naming convention (`in.encoding`/`out.encoding` style used elsewhere, like `"out.dir"`). Since `getReportProperty` looks up properties by these keys, it never found the actual configured encoding values, causing `m_outputEncoding`/`m_sourceEncoding` to remain null, which later propagated null encodings to report generators.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
